To: Drago Pinteric <drago.pinteric@bureauveritas.com>; Yoshiyuki Sugihara <yoshiyuki.sugihara@bureauveritas.com>; Christophe VAES <christophe.vaes@bureauveritas.com>; Wayne Hamilton <wayne.hamilton@bureauveritas.com>
Subject: TOCA Out


Dear Gents,



Following the TOCA OUT / GT leakage slide, I would like to ask you to prepare a more detailed YTD overview for your area covering the period from the beginning of this year until today.



We need to better understand the reasons behind the vessels leaving BV (except CD change) and identify any common patterns or areas where we need to take action. Please prepare the analysis mainly for tankers, bulk carriers and gas carriers, and, if the data is available, also include the other vessel types.



For each vessel, please provide as far as possible:



  *   Vessel name and vessel type
  *   Age/year built
  *   GT
  *   Owner/account
  *   Person responsible for the account from the marketing/commercial side
  *   Date of TOCA OUT
  *   Reason why the vessel left BV
  *   Whether it was related to Owner decision, commercial/pricing issue, service/performance issue, change of ownership, sale/scrapping, competitor approach, or any other reason
  *   Any additional background or comments which may help us understand the case



[cid:image006.png@01DD5036.9A0D1E70]





[cid:image001.gif@01DD5036.38420610]<https://group.bureauveritas.com/>

